# 🚀 Career Management System (React + Google Apps Script + Google Sheets + Google Drive)

A modern, serverless **Career Management System** built with **React JS**, **Google Apps Script API**, **Google Sheets** for data storage, and **Google Drive** for resume storage. 

> [!TIP]
> **No PHP server or MySQL database required!** 100% free, reliable, and maintenance-free infrastructure powered by Google Workspace.

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph LR
    User[React Candidate Form] -->|Base64 Resume + Form Data| GAS[Google Apps Script Web App]
    GAS -->|Store Resume PDF/DOCX| Drive[Google Drive Folder]
    GAS -->|Append Candidate Record| Sheet[Google Sheets Database]
    Drive -->|Generates View URL| GAS
    GAS -->|Returns Application ID| User
```

---

## 📁 Files Created in Codebase

1. **`gas/Code.gs`**: The Google Apps Script backend script.
2. **`src/services/googleCareerService.js`**: React service for Base64 encoding and API submission.
3. **`src/components/Career/ApplicationModal.jsx`**: Frontend candidate application modal with resume uploader.

---

## ⚙️ Step-by-Step Setup Guide (2 Minutes)

### Step 1: Open Google Apps Script
1. Go to [script.google.com](https://script.google.com) and click **+ New project**.
2. Rename the project to **`Anthem Career System API`**.

### Step 2: Paste the Backend Code
1. Open [gas/Code.gs](file:///c:/Users/aaron/OneDrive/Desktop/Anthem/anthem%202nd%20project/anthem-diagnostics/gas/Code.gs).
2. Copy the entire script and paste it into the Google Apps Script code editor.
3. Click the **Save** icon (💾 or `Ctrl + S`).

### Step 3: Deploy as Web App
1. In the top right corner, click **Deploy** ➔ **New deployment**.
2. Click the gear icon (⚙️) next to *Select type* and select **Web app**.
3. Fill in the deployment details:
   - **Description**: `Career System API v1`
   - **Execute as**: **`Me (your_email@gmail.com)`**
   - **Who has access**: **`Anyone`** *(Crucial for public form submissions)*
4. Click **Deploy**.
5. Grant the required permissions (Authorize access to Google Drive and Google Sheets when prompted).
6. Copy the generated **Web App URL** (starts with `https://script.google.com/macros/s/.../exec`).

### Step 4: Connect Web App URL to React
In your React application root directory, open or create your `.env` file and set:

```env
VITE_GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/YOUR_DEPLOYED_SCRIPT_ID/exec
```

*(Alternatively, paste the URL directly into `src/services/googleCareerService.js`)*

---

## 📊 Automatic Database Creation

Upon receiving the first job application:
- **Google Sheets**: Automatically creates a spreadsheet named **`Anthem Job Applications`** with formatted column headers:
  - `Application ID`, `Submitted At`, `Full Name`, `Email Address`, `Phone Number`, `Job Title`, `Department`, `Preferred Location`, `Resume File Name`, `Google Drive Resume Link`, `Message`, `Status`.
- **Google Drive**: Automatically creates a folder named **`Anthem Job Resumes`** and sets sharing permissions so recruiters can view resumes directly via clickable links.

---

## 🔒 Security & Reliability Features

- **No-CORS & Fail-Safe Architecture**: If the Google Apps Script URL is missing or unreachable, the system automatically saves a backup copy to local storage (`applicationsStorage.js`), ensuring zero data loss.
- **Direct Base64 Upload**: Converts PDFs and DOCX files client-side before sending to Google Apps Script.
